spiraling horrors a gender-bent riff on  shakespeare and a whole series about  camping here's a few upcoming titles  that anime fans are looking forward to  in 2022  anime and horror fans got some very  welcome news in october 2019 when adult  swim announced it was turning junji  ito's terrifying masterpiece uzumaki  into a four-part mini-series the beloved  late 90s manga received a live-action  adaptation in 2000 that got mixed  reviews but if anyone can pull off an  animated take on ito's supernatural tale  it's hiroshi nakahama  nagahama best known for turning the  trippy horror manga mushishi into a  highly rated hit has big plans for  uzumaki in the first teaser for the show  nagahama stated his artistic vision i  wanted to make something that scares  people and makes them laugh and that  they'll watch over and over that's the  kind of work i want this to be  nagahama's promises got fans of ido's  manga excited but the original 2020  release date came and went without a  premiere in 2021 adult swim confirmed  that uzumaki was still in progress and  would drop the following year nagahama  told fans i feel truly apologetic for  the delay and ask for your patience just  a little more uzumaki which translates  to spiral takes place in a small  japanese town where a supernatural curse  is wreaking havoc production ig the  studio responsible for ghost in the  shell has been making strong efforts to  adapt ito's art style to the screen as  faithfully as possible  funimation teamed up with fox to release  2018's dragon ball super broly in  theaters across 18 different countries  and it proved to be a wise move the film  raked in over 115 million dollars at the  worldwide box office and earned rave  reviews from critics becoming a hit even  with viewers unfamiliar with the  franchise there has been a renewed  interest in all things dragon ball since  the sequel series dragon ball super  began airing in 2015 and the fan base is  now bigger than ever fans who grew up  watching the original 80s anime are now  sharing it with their children creating  what funimation's mitchell burger calls  quote multi-generational appeal this was  reflected in the rapturous response to  dragon ball super broly which gave the  titular saiyan a new and improved origin  story it was so well received in fact  that series creator akira toriyama  confirmed that a new film dragon ball  super superhero was in the pipeline for  2022 it's about time  toriyama hyped up the film on the  official dragon ball website writing  just like the previous movie i'm heavily  leading the story and dialogue  production i really shouldn't talk too  much about the plot yet but be prepared  for some extreme and entertaining bouts  which may feature an unexpected  character the film's title and updated  character designs were revealed at  comic-con at home 2021.  what's cooler than a guy with a chainsaw  a guy who is a chainsaw tatsuki  fujimoto's action fantasy chainsaw man  made waves when it hit shelves in  december 2018. mappa the studio behind  dora hiduro and jujutsu kaizen was quick  to take on the challenge of adapting the  high octane manga denji is a devil  hunter buried in debt barely scraping by  with his devil dog fuchita when a job  gone wrong ends with the yakuza  literally backstabbing him genji makes a  deal with pogita that allows him to be  reborn as a human devil hybrid by  pulling the cord on his chest deji can  become the chainsaw devil a monster with  multiple chainsaws emerging from his  head and arms known for its brutal  fights and dark humor the chainsaw man  manga won the 2020 shogakucan award for  best shonen while an exact release date  has yet to be determined a recent  trailer confirms that fans can expect to  see the bloody affair on the small  screen in 2022  the hit 2020 anime moriarty the patriot  offered a new take on a classic literary  character and another radically  different version of a famous villain is  slated to hit the small screen in 2022  only this time it's one that actually  existed  ayakano's manga series requiem for the  rose king follows a gender fluid version  of richard iii one of the most hated  monarchs in history the show takes place  in the period known as the war of the  roses a 30-year conflict between the  noble houses of york and lancaster when  the story begins richard's father is  closing in on the throne but it's not to  be the duke of york has the crown and  his life snatched away before he can  claim it the loss of his father hits  richard hard the bloody conflict rages  on however and with his beloved dad now  gone richard's thoughts turned to  revenge and ultimately the throne  loosely based on the classic shakespeare  play richard iii the manga debuted in  monthly princess magazine in 2013 and is  still going strong today known for being  full of unexpected twists and turns  requiem of the rose king will no doubt  make for a fascinating anime series when  it drops in january 2022  the rising of the shield hero was one of  the most popular anime of 2019 but it  was also one of the most controversial  on paper it's just a standard isekai a  fantasy subgenre in which the  protagonist is suddenly transported to a  strange new world it's difficult for  nuisakai shows to stand out from the  incredibly large crowd but the rising of  the shield hero managed to do so in an  incredibly bold and risky way after  arriving in his fantasy world the  protagonist is falsely accused of sexual  assault socially ineptotaku naofumi  watani is one of four regular people  summoned to the kingdom of melromark to  save it from impending doom dubbed the  four cardinal heroes each receives a  legendary weapon to help them in their  quest now fumi's weapon being a shield  when his training partner betrays him  with a treacherous lie now fumi becomes  an outcast setting out to combat the  waves of calamity on his own some people  took issue with the show's use of a  sexual assault accusation as a plot  device but fans have been clamoring for  a second season ever since the first one  wrapped  the fact that a couple of cuckoos has  become one of the most anticipated anime  of 2022 is quite remarkable considering  how new the manga that it's based on is  written and illustrated by miki  yoshikawa a couple of cuckoos is massive  in japan two volumes of the cutesy  romcom were sold every second during the  height of its popularity and fans can't  wait to see how director yoshiyuki  shirahara handles the story as the  teaser trailer for the show reveals a  couple of cuckoo's is a love story about  a shy boy and an internet famous girl  introverted high school student nagi  umino is on the way to meet his  biological parents for the first time  when he encounters erica amano a social  media star trying to escape an arranged  marriage she proposes that nagi become  her fake boyfriend so she doesn't have  to go through with it and he reluctantly  agrees they soon discover that nagi is  actually her intended husband after all  they were accidentally switched as  babies and the parents believe a wedding  is the best way they can be a proper  family unfortunately for them nagi has  his eye on someone else and chaos ensues  another show that was pushed back to  2022 because of the coronavirus pandemic  spriggan is collaboration between  netflix and david production for those  unfamiliar with the title spriggan is a  shonen sci-fi manga that ran from 1989  to 1986 and got a movie adaptation in  1998. spriggan takes place in an  alternate reality version of the cold  war in which mankind has discovered the  existence of advanced tech hidden by an  ancient civilization making sure these  gadgets don't fall into the wrong hands  is you ominae a member of an elite unit  that takes on militias and assorted bad  guys with ulterior motives netflix has  already dropped a couple of teaser  trailers for spriggan and they look  great david production knows all about  flamboyance this is the studio behind  jojo's bizarre adventure after all but  they're wisely keeping things sleek and  simple with this particular project  hiroshi kobayashi who has directed  episodes of kizu naiver and tiger and  bunny is overseeing the action  well you can color me impressed  at a glance made in abyss looks like the  kind of show you could comfortably watch  with children but the 2017 adventure  series is far from a family-friendly  affair based on akihito takushi's manga  series of the same name made in abyss  follows an orphan girl named rico who  lives in a town built around a giant  gaping hole referred to as you guessed  it the abyss all manner of strange  artifacts and creatures are said to be  found inside though few are brave enough  to explore its depths those who enter  the hole are known as cave raiders one  of whom was rico's mother although she  seemingly vanished during an expedition  it turns out she may not be gone after  all when rico finds a message from her  mother urging her to meet her in the  abyss she decides that it's time to  explore it for herself with the help of  a new robot friend  season two of made in abyss was  announced in 2019 and a film entitled  dawn of the deep soul dropped the  following year the story is set to  continue in 2022 when the second season  officially titled made in abyss the sun  blazes upon the golden city will come to  air plot details are being kept mostly  under wraps for now but at least one  previously unseen character will appear  manga readers will no doubt recognize  the fluffy white arms of faputa princess  of the naharati  the global phenomenon that was the  attack on titan manga came to an end  when the final chapter shipped in  basatsu shonen magazine in summer 2021  for anime viewers however the journey  doesn't reach its conclusion until 2022  when the second part of the fourth and  final season is set to air attack on  titan's fans became worried when it was  revealed that wit studio would no longer  produce the show after season 3 but mapa  stepped in and exceeded expectations  season 3 of attack on titan ended on a  rare high note for our heroes who got to  see the ocean for the first time but  things were far from rosy when we caught  up with him in attack on titan the final  season part 1. there's a four-year time  jump between the seasons and protagonist  aaron yeager isn't the same man he once  was noticeably older the veteran of the  survey corps has been worn down by the  rigors of war as have his comrades  there's trouble with the country across  the sea marley is at war with the  aldians the descendants of the first  titan aaron also has an old acquaintance  to worry about the part one finale ended  just as he was about to face former  friend reiner braun in battle attack on  titan the final season part 2 will begin  on january 9th 2022  a live action movie adaptation of the  original anime series tiger and bunny  was announced in 2015 with ron howard  attached as a producer despite the fact  that superhero movies have only grown in  popularity there's been little movement  since however fans of tiger and bunny  need not despair their decade long wait  for a second season of the original show  is soon to become a reality sunrise the  studio behind the original tiger and  bunny has confirmed that the highly  anticipated follow-up season entitled  tiger and bunny 2 will come to air at  some point in 2022 tiger and bunny takes  place in a far future city called  sternbuild which is rife with both crime  and superheroes wearing costumes  plastered in sponsors the vigilantes of  sternbuild take part in a show called  hero tv competing against each other by  earning points for every crime they stop  whoever earns the most points is crowned  the king of heroes but not all of them  care about fame and prestige we follow  veteran superhero kotetsu wild tiger  kabaragi and his rookie partner barnby  bunny brooks jr two men who have very  different opinions about what it means  to be a hero  influential 80s anime captain tsubasa  got a brand new season in 2018  reigniting interest in soccer shows in  2022 another fictional japanese player  will make the leap from the pages of his  manga to the small screen ali ashito the  protagonist of yugo kobayashi's aoashi  aoi has plenty of raw talent but needs  some work if he's going to make it all  the way to the jailey japan's premier  soccer division luckily coach tatsuya  fukuda is willing to put the work in  after recognizing his potential the  former pro invites ali to a training  camp for tokyo city's aspirin fc's youth  team like all the other animated soccer  stars that came before him aoi  revolutionizes the sport in japan but  what makes aoashi different is that it's  relatively new and therefore much in  tune with the modern game the action in  captain tsubasa is often so exaggerated  that it barely resembles real soccer but  she takes the sport seriously with  characters learning formations and  executing plays that you would see in an  actual real life game it's the manga  that soccer fans have been waiting for  and the anime adaptation is dropping at  the perfect time it's scheduled for  release during the spring 2022 season  meaning it will be on air in the run-up  to the fifa world cup  from calligraphy to mineralogy to  fishing and ballroom dancing there's an  anime for just about every hobby based  on the slice of life manga of the same  name laid back camp caters to lovers of  camping following a group of friends who  traveled to different sites across japan  it's a delightfully simple story that  made for a charming anime when studio c  station adapted it for the small screen  in 2018 there's also a live action tv  remake for fans to check out but what  they really want is more anime and  that's exactly what they're getting in  2022 as the promotional poster reveals  the laid-back campgrounds are returning  for an anime movie along with the  creators that made the anime series such  a success screenwriters jintanaka and  mitsumi ido are back as is director  yoshiaki kyogoku whose work on laid back  camp earned him an award at the tokyo  anime film festival kyogoku told anime  news network i like to think that the  award went to the show and not to me  while the show is good it's not mine it  was all the staff's hard work that made  it possible i would like to think that  the award came to me as a representative  of the show and not me personally check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite anime are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

